WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
So why don't people see the gap sooner?

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:05.012
Because it's invisible until
a design depends on it.

3
00:00:05.012 --> 00:00:11.276
The surfaces are shared: Intune in GCC is
the same instance as commercial Intune.

4
00:00:11.276 --> 00:00:14.987
The exclusions are scattered,
one sentence per feature page.

5
00:00:14.987 --> 00:00:17.188
And absence doesn't announce itself.

6
00:00:17.188 --> 00:00:21.388
A detection whose input never arrives
looks exactly like a quiet day.

7
00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:24.429
The book then tests a
widely repeated example,

8
00:00:24.429 --> 00:00:27.711
that five features are
silently missing from GCC.

9
00:00:27.711 --> 00:00:31.394
Checked against Microsoft's
documentation, only one is:

10
00:00:31.394 --> 00:00:35.637
the Locations view of network
connectivity in the admin center.

11
00:00:35.637 --> 00:00:39.258
The others turn out to be
GCC High and DoD gaps,

12
00:00:39.258 --> 00:00:43.563
not documented gaps at all,
or inside Azure's own scope.

13
00:00:43.563 --> 00:00:46.912
The lesson: an unverified
boundary story sends an

14
00:00:46.912 --> 00:00:50.262
agency off to build
compensations it doesn't need.

15
00:00:50.262 --> 00:00:53.180
Now, what actually
changes across a boundary.
